    "story": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The House of EvlveX",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>EvlveX is a house of shoes made by hand, and every one of them begins as a story. A seaside court at dusk. A river walked every Sunday. A night train arriving at dawn. We keep the story close while we cut, stitch and finish, until the shoe can carry it.</p><p>Each model is a chapter of the house, numbered in the order it was told. Each pair then gains a chapter of its own: who finished it, the day they did, and finally the name of the person who will wear it further. That is the promise in our name. A well-made pair evolves with its owner, and its story goes on.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": ["heading", "text"],
      "settings": {
        "desktop_content_position": "center",
        "content_alignment": "center",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-1",
        "full_width": false,
        "padding_top": 96,
        "padding_bottom": 80
      }
    },
    "atelier": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "caption": {
          "type": "caption",
          "settings": {
            "caption": "The Atelier",
            "text_style": "caption-with-letter-spacing",
            "text_size": "small"
          }
        },
        "heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Cut, stitched and finished by hand",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A pair passes through few hands, and each one leaves something. The cutter reads the hide and chooses where the story will sit. The stitcher sets the seams that will hold it. The finisher burnishes, laces and inspects, then signs the pair as their own.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": ["caption", "heading", "text"],
      "settings": {
        "height": "large",
        "desktop_image_width": "medium",
        "layout": "image_first",
        "image_behavior": "none",
        "content_layout": "no-overlap",
        "desktop_content_position": "middle",
        "desktop_content_alignment": "left",
        "mobile_content_alignment": "left",
        "section_color_scheme": "scheme-2",
        "color_scheme": "scheme-2",
        "padding_top": 0,
        "padding_bottom": 0
      }
    },
    "workshop-card": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "caption": {
          "type": "caption",
          "settings": {
            "caption": "The Workshop Card",
            "text_style": "caption-with-letter-spacing",
            "text_size": "small"
          }
        },
        "heading": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Each pair's own chapter, written by hand",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>When a pair leaves the bench, its artisan writes a card: the pair's number, the day it was finished, and one true line about this pair alone, perhaps the hide it was cut from, or the grain across the toe. The card travels in the box. The same words are written into the pair's certificate, under your name.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        },
